# Milestone: M3
# Covers: a call and its return inside a loop body do not let a strand run
#         past its step's budget -- the loop's backward jump is still the
#         safepoint -- and a call chain with no loop spends no budget.
# matrix-row: scheduler-safepoint
#
# The legacy record claimed a safepoint at every call-frame push and pop.
# This core spends the instruction budget on backward jumps only
# (docs/internals/runtime.md), so what is observable, and pinned here, is
# the two halves of that rule.  The work runs in an `at` body so that it
# starts in a `step` the fixture sizes, as budget_step_exhausted.chk does.
#
# 1. A 20000-round loop whose body is a call: a budget of 1 comes back
#    RUNNING with the work unfinished; a large budget finishes it.
# 2. A 200-deep recursion with no loop: a budget of 1 finishes it.
## timeout: 30
## host: run var x = 0
## host: run var y = 0
## host: run var done = 0
## host: run var f = function(n) { n + 1 }
## host: run var r = function(n) { if (n == 0) 0 else r(n - 1) }
## host: run at (x > 0) { var i = 0; while (i < 20000) { i = f(i) }; done = 1 }
## host: run at (y > 0) { r(200); done = 2 }
## host: set-global x 1
## host: step 1
## host: run done
## host: step 1000000
## host: run done
## host: set-global y 1
## host: step 1
## host: run done
[00000000] 0
[00000000] 0
[00000000] 0
[00000000] <?>
[00000000] <?>
[00000000] nil
[00000000] nil
[00000000] set-global: ok
[00000000] step: RUNNING
[00000000] 0
[00000000] step: QUIESCENT
[00000000] 1
[00000000] set-global: ok
[00000000] step: QUIESCENT
[00000000] 2
